--AHDL2PLA--
*Comment,A
$Header: /swpg/develop/dsp/src/ui/abel/abel5/RCS/abelerr.mnu,v 9.24 1993/09/03 20:33:45 jan Exp $
*Global Keys,A
Global Keys
    <<F1>>          Context sensitive, multi-level help    
    <<ESC>>         Toggles between Editor Window and Menu Bar  
    <<^L>>          Redraw screen
    <<_Alt-l>>etter Pops up menu with highlighted character that
                matches letter
*==Errors Help==,A
*--AHDL2PLA--,A
*1000,A

Command Error 1000: ABEL needs an ABEL-HDL source file to be specified.

An ABEL-HDL source file is expected as the input to AHDL2PLA. The
file should be specified as the first argument to the AHDL2PLA
program.

*1001,A

Syntax Error 1001:  String expected.

A string argument was expected in the indicated location in the
source file. A string is a sequence of one or more characters
delimited by ' (single-quote) or ` (back-quote) characters.

*1002,A

Logical Error 1002:  Source line length exceeds nn characters.

Individual lines of an ABEL-HDL source file cannot exceed the
indicated number of characters. 

*1003,A

Fatal Error 1003:  Unable to open input file 'xxxx'.

The indicated file could not be opened by AHDL2PLA. If the indicated
file exists, check to make sure that it has the appropriate file
protection settings to enable you to access it.

*1004,A

Warning 1004:  FLAGS statement obsolete - mapping old flags to new
options.

The FLAGS statement, used in previous versions of ABEL, has been
replaced with the OPTIONS statement in ABEL-HDL. In most cases the
old flags specified in a FLAGS statement can be automatically
mapped to the proper options.

*1005,A

Syntax Error 1005:  Identifier length exceeds nn characters.

Identifiers (module, device, signal and constant names) must not
exceed the indicated length.

*1006,A

Syntax Error 1006:  Undefined sequence of characters encountered.

An unrecognized sequence of non-alphabetic characters was
encountered in the source file.

*1007,A

Syntax Error 1007:  String length exceeds nn characters.

A string was encountered that exceeds the maximum allowable number
of characters. This is usually an indication that the terminating
string delimiter was unintentionally omitted.

*1008,A

Syntax Error 1008:  Only ^b, ^o, ^d or ^h radix allowed.

The ^ (circumflex) character was encountered in the source file with
an unknown radix character immediately following it.

*1009,A

Syntax Error 1009:  Can't have letters imbedded in a number.

An unsupported sequence of numeric and alphabetic characters was
encountered in the source file.

*1010,A

Logical Error 1010:  Numeric overflow.

An operation performed on constant values resulted in a number
larger than supported.

*1011,A

Syntax Error 1011:  Actual argument length exceeds nn characters.

An actual argument (the text passed as an argument to a macro or
module) exceeds the indicated maximum number of characters.

*1012,A

Syntax Error 1012:  Macro or Module called with more actual
arguments than the nn declared.

The macro or module being processed has the indicated number of
dummy arguments declared, and the macro or module was called with
too many actual arguments.

*1013,A

Warning 1013:  Attribute 'FEED_OR' is obsolete - substituting '.D'
instead.

The 'FEED_OR' signal attribute was used in previous versions of ABEL
to specify the feedback configuration for the indicated signal. In
ABEL-HDL, the feedback path is specified as a part of the related
design description by using dot extensions. The appropriate dot
extension to indicate the combinational feedback path from a
registered output is typically '.D', so this dot extension will be
appended to all affected signals when they are referenced as inputs.

*1014,A

Warning 1014:  Attribute 'FEED_PIN' is obsolete - substituting
'.PIN' instead.

The 'FEED_PIN' signal attribute was used in previous versions of
ABEL to specify the feedback configuration for the indicated signal.
In ABEL-HDL, the feedback path is specified as a part of the related
design description by using dot extensions. The appropriate dot
extension to indicated the feedback path from an output pin is
'.PIN', so this dot extension will be appended to all affected
signals when they are referenced as inputs.

*1015,A

Warning 1015:  Attribute 'FEED_REG' is obsolete - substituting '.FB'
instead.

The 'FEED_REG' signal attribute was used in previous versions of
ABEL to specify the feedback configuration for the indicated signal.
In ABEL-HDL, the feedback path is specified as a part of the related
design description by using dot extensions. The appropriate dot
extension to indicated the registered feedback path is typically
'.FB', so this dot extension will be appended to all affected
signals when they are referenced as inputs.

*1016,A

Fatal Error 1016:  Unable to open output file 'xxxx'.

The indicated file could not be opened. This can indicate a full
disk drive, invalid path, or file protection problems.

*1017,A

Syntax Error 1017:  ENDCASE expected.

A CASE transition statement was not terminated with an ENDCASE
statement.

*1018,A

Warning Error 1018:  No register type specified for 'xxxx' - please
use ISTYPE.

The indicated signal has not been declared with a register type. If
no device and pin number have been declared, you should use the
ISTYPE statement to specify that the signal is either combinational
(ISTYPE 'COM') or registered (ISTYPE 'REG' or ISTYPE 'REG_x' where
x is either D, T, SR, JK, JKD, L or G).

*1019,A

Syntax Error 1019:  Keyword 'xxxx' expected.

The indicated keyword was expected in the source file.

*1020,A

Syntax Error 1020:  Identifier expected.

An identifier (module, device, signal or constant name) was expected
in the source file.

*1021,A

Syntax Error 1021:  Undefined compiler directive '@xxxx'.

An '@' sign was encountered that was followed by an unknown 
directive name.

*1022,A

Syntax Error 1022:  Special constant must end with a '.'.

Special constants are delimited by '.' (period) characters. This
error can also indicated incorrect usage of dot extensions, which
are prefixed by '.' characters.

*1023,A

Syntax Error 1023:  Undefined special constant 'xxxx'.

An unknown special constant was found delimited by '.' (period)
characters.

*1024,A

Syntax Error 1024:  Label expected.

A label was expected in the source file. A label is a sequence of
alphanumeric characters that does not begin with a number, and is
not an ABEL-HDL reserved word (keyword).

*1025,A

Syntax Error 1025:  Can't use ':=' operator with dot extension
signal 'xxxx'.

The ':=' (registered assignment) operator is used to indicated a
pin-to-pin relationship between an input expression and a
corresponding registered output pin. Dot extension signals are
inherently combinational, and should therefore be described with the
'=' (unclocked assignment) operator.

*1026,A

Syntax Error 1026:  ';' expected.

A semicolon was expected in the source file.

*1027,A

Syntax Error 1027:  Module label doesn't match 'xxxx'.

The END statement was followed by a module name that does not match
the module name specified in the previous MODULE statement.

*1028,A

Syntax Error 1028:  EQUATIONS, STATE_DIAGRAM, TRUTH_TABLE or END
expected.

A keyword was encountered out of place in the source file. This can
indicate any number of syntax problems, including misplaced or 
missing semicolons or parenthesis, unbalanced IF-THEN, WHEN-THEN or
CASE statements, or earlier syntax problems.

*1029,A

Syntax Error 1029:  PIN, NODE, DEVICE, ISTYPE, MACRO or '='
expected.

A label, keyword or operator was encountered out of place in the 
declarations section of the source file. This error often
results if a comma is omitted from a list of identifiers.

*1030,A

Warning 1030:  Inconsistency in number of parameters.

A constant declaration statement had an unbalanced number of items
on the right and left side of the '=' (constant assignment)
operator.

*1031,A

Syntax Error 1031:  Undefined label 'xxxx'.

A label was referenced that was not declared in a declarations
section of the source file.

*1032,A

Syntax Error 1032:  Signal not allowed.

A signal was not allowed as an operand or argument in the indicated
expression.

*1033,A

Syntax Error 1033:  Maximum of nn elements in set was exceeded.

Set widths are restricted to 128 elements.

*1034,A

Syntax Error 1034:  ']' expected.

A set was not terminated with a ']' (right bracket) delimiter
character.

*1035,A

Syntax Error 1035:  Unsupported operation on special constant.

Special constants are not supported as operands in the indicated
expression.

*1036,A

Syntax Error 1036:  Can't compare set with nn members to one with nn
members.

Set widths must match when performing operations on two sets.

*1037,A

Syntax Error 1037:  ')' expected.

The ')' (right parenthesis) character was expected as a delimiter.

*1038,A

Syntax Error 1038:  Pin number, ISTYPE or ';' expected.

A signal (PIN or NODE) declaration is not complete.  Usually a
semicolon needs to be added to the end of the declaration.

*1039,A

Syntax Error 1039:  Label 'xxxx' is already defined.

The indicated label was already used in a previous declaration. 
This can indicate a missing or misplaced EQUATIONS keyword.

*1040,A

Syntax Error 1040:  Number expected.

A number was expected in the source file. Numbers can be entered
as decimal values, prefixed by a radix specification, or can be
specified as a set of binary values.

*1041,A

Syntax Error 1041:  Keyword 'xxxx' is out of context.

The indicated keyword was used in an unsupported manner.

*1042,A

Logical Error 1042:  END expected.

The end of the source file was encountered before an END statement
was found. 

*1043,A

Warning 1043:  Register type mismatch for output 'xxxx'.

The indicated output was declared with a register type that
conflicts with the dot extensions used, or the design was written
using ':=' equations but the indicated register was not declared as
'reg'. The ':=' (clocked assignment) operator is intended for use
with D-type flip-flops only. For alternate flip-flop types, use
the '=' (combinational assignment) operator in conjunction with
either a .T, .J, .K, .S, .R, or other register input port dot
extension.

*1045,A

Warning 1045:  'INVERT' or 'BUFFER' not specified for 'xxxx' -
output uncertain.

An output signal has been described using a register input dot
extension (.D, .T, .J, .K, .S, or .R) but the associated
output signal has not been declared with an 'INVERT' or 'BUFFER'
attribute. Since there is no information about the existence of an
inverter between the register and the associated output pin, the
actual value observed on that pin is uncertain.

*1046,A

Syntax Error 1046:  Can't operate on signal 'xxxx'.

The indicated signal was used in an expression in which only numbers
or constant values are allowed.

*1047,A

Syntax Error 1047:  signal or .X. expected.

A declared signal (pin or node) or the special constant '.X.' was
expected in the source file.

*1048,A

Syntax Error 1048:  '=' or ':=' expected.

An assignment operator was expected in the source file.

*1049,A

Syntax Error 1049:  expression element expected.

An expression was expected in the source file. Expressions are
composed of one or more signals, sets, numbers or special constants
operated on by supported ABEL-HDL operators. Expressions can be
enclosed in parenthesis.

*1050,A

Warning 1050:  'INVERT' or 'BUFFER' not specified for 'xxxx' -
feedback uncertain.

Feedback from a registered signal has been described using the '.Q'
dot extension, but the associated output signal has not been
declared with an 'INVERT' or 'BUFFER' attribute. Since there is no
information about the existence of an inverter between the register
and the associated output pin, the relationship between the value
observed on that pin and the value fed back from the register is
uncertain.


*1051,A

Syntax Error 1051:  GOTO, IF or CASE expected.

A state transition (GOTO, IF-THEN-ELSE, or CASE) statement was
expected.

*1052,A

Syntax Error 1052:  THEN expected.

The THEN portion of an IF-THEN-ELSE statement was omitted.

*1053,A

Syntax Error 1053:  Signal 'xxxx' is combinational.

The ':=' (clocked assignment) operator was used to describe a signal
that was declared as combinational.

*1054,A

Syntax Error 1054:  '(' expected.

A '(' (left parenthesis) character was expected as a delimiter.

*1055,A

Syntax Error 1055:  '->' expected

The '->' operator was expected to delimit the input and output
portions of a truth table or test vector header or entry.

*1056,A

Logical Error 1056:  Extension 'xxxx' is not supported for node
'xxxx'.

The indicated dot extension is not appropriate for the indicated
node.

*1057,A

Syntax Error 1057:  Cannot map set onto a non-set element.

A set was specified in a test vector where a single-bit value was
expected.

*1058,A

Syntax Error 1058:  Special constant not allowed.

Special constants are not allowed in the current context.  Special
constants are surrounded by periods (for example, .c.), so this
error can indicate an improper use of a period.

*1059,A

Syntax Error 1059:  Undefined operation on sets.

Sets may not be used as operands of '>>' (shift right), '<<'
(shift left), '*' (multiply), '/' (divide) or '%' (modulo)
operators.

*1060,A

Syntax Error 1060:  Cannot map set onto a different sized set.

Set widths must match when performing operations on two sets, or
when using nested sets in truth tables or test vectors.

*1061,A

Warning 1061:  No output type specified for 'xxxx' - use ISTYPE.

You have used the indicated signal as an output, but have not
declared whether it is combinational or registered.

*1062,A

Warning 1062:  Extension 'xxxx' may not be supported for signal
'xxxx'.

You have used a dot extension that does not match the known dot
extensions for the output type declared for the indicated signal.

*1063,A

Syntax Error 1063:  Dummy argument 'xxxx' not recognized.

A dummy argument (indicated by prefixing a label with the '?'
character) has been used that does not match the dummy arguments
declared in the macro or module argument list.

*1064,A

Syntax Error 1064:  Signal number for 'xxxx' exceeds the maximum 
supported by this device.

You have specified a pin or node number that is not found on the 
specified device, or have specified a very large pin number.

*1065,A

Syntax Error 1065:  Pin number nn is not defined for this
device.

You have specified a pin number that is undefined for the declared
device.

*1066,A

Syntax Error 1066:  Node number nn is not defined for this device.

You have specified a node number that is undefined for the declared
device.

*1067,A

Syntax Error 1067:  Only one label allowed for each macro.

You have specified a list of labels in a macro definition. Only one
label is allowed for each macro.

*1068,A

Syntax Error 1068:  Block expected.

A block was expected following a macro keyword or directive. A block
is a section of ABEL-HDL source statements enclosed by braces.

*1069,A

Syntax Error 1069:  Terminating '}' delimiter expected.

A terminating '}' (right brace) delimiter was not found in the
source file.

*1070,A

Warning 1070:  Pin number nn is already declared as 'xxxx'.

You have declared the same pin number for two different named
signals.

*1071,A

Syntax Error 1071:  Closing ''' of string not found.

The terminating ' (single quote) character was omitted from a
string. This error can occur if a single quote (or back quote)
character is imbedded in a string without being prefixed by a
'\' (backslash) character.

*1072,A

Syntax Error 1072:  ':+:' or ':*:' expected.

You have specified @ALTERNATE (use alternate operators) and have
specified an XOR or XNOR operation in an unsupported way.

*1073,A

Syntax Error 1073:  Constant label expected.

The @CONST directive requires a constant label. This label must not
have been previously declared (as a signal, macro or other 
identifier) except that it can be used in previous @CONST directive
statement.

*1074,A

Syntax Error 1074:  '=' expected.

The '=' (assignment operator) was omitted from an @CONST directive
or from a fuse assignment statement.

*1075,A

Syntax Error 1075:  Undefined operation on signal.

A signal identifier is not supported in the current context.

*1076,A

Syntax Error 1076:  Number is too large.

Numbers (either literal values or values produced by complex
expressions) cannot exceed the maximum size of 128 bits (unsigned).

*1077,A

Syntax Error 1077:  ':>' or '->' expected.

The ':>' or '->' operator was expected to delimit the input and
output portions of a truth table header or entry line.

*1078,A

Syntax Error 1078:  ':>' expected.

The ':>' operator was expected in a truth table entry line to match
the ':>' operator found in the truth table header.

*1079,A

Syntax Error 1079:  Radix nn is not one of 2, 8, 10 or 16.

The radix value specified in a @RADIX statement must be either 2
(binary), 8 (octal), 10 (decimal) or 16 (hexadecimal).

*1080,A

Syntax Error 1080:  nn actual arguments expected.

A macro or module was invoked with a different number of actual
arguments than that declared in the macro or module.

*1081,A

Syntax Error 1081:  Dummy argument expected.

The '?' character indicates that the following sequence of
characters is a dummy argument. The error indicates that the dummy
argument label does not match any of the dummy arguments listed in
the macro or module declaration.

*1082,A

Syntax Error 1082:  Digit not in radix nn.

You have specified a radix value less than 10 (decimal) and have
used a digit that is not supported in that number system.

*1083,A

Warning 1083:  Signal 'xxxx' is declared as registered.

The indicated signal was declared as a registered output, but was
used as a combinational output.

*1084,A

Warning 1084:  Unrecognized attribute 'xxxx' - attribute ignored.

The attribute string specified in an ISTYPE statement was not
recognized as a supported signal attribute.

*1085,A

Warning 1085:  'xxxx' attribute not supported on this pin.

The specified attribute is not supported for the device and pin or
node number indicated, or the attribute conflicts with a previous
attribute specified for the same signal.  The attribute will be
ignored.

*1086,A

Warning 1086:  Signal 'xxxx' has not been declared as combinational.

You have written a combinational function for the indicated signal,
but have not specified that the signal is combinational (ISTYPE
'COM').

*1087,A

Warning 1087:  Signal 'xxxx' has not been declared as registered.

You have written a registered (pin-to-pin) function for the
indicated signal, but have not declared the signal as registered
(ISTYPE 'REG' or ISTYPE 'REG_X' where X is a register type).

*1088,A

Syntax Error 1088:  Symbolic state register name not supported in
this context.

Symbolic state names (declared with the STATE_REGISTER declaration)
are not supported in the type of expression indicated.

*1089,A

Syntax Error 1089:  'xxxx' is already defined.

The indicated identifier name was previously declared.  

*1090,A

Warning 1090:  Using .Q with ':=' or ISTYPE 'reg' state diagrams is
not recommended - use .FB for feedback.

*1091,A

Logical Error 1091:  nn actual arguments specified on command line.

The number of actual arguments specified on the AHDL2PLA command
line exceeds the number of dummy arguments specified in the MODULE
statement.

*1092,A

Syntax Error 1092:  Use '#' for OR instead of '|'.

The '|' operator (used in some programming languages for a bitwise
OR) is not used in ABEL-HDL. Use the '#' operator.

*1093,A

Syntax Error 1093:  Default value must be a number or .X.

Default values specified in INTERFACE statements must be either 1, 0
or some other numeric value.

*1094,A

Syntax Error 1094:  No operators allowed in this context.

You have attempted to use a complex expression (one containing
operators) when only signals, numbers or special constants are
supported. This error most frequently occurs when dot extensions are
applied to complex expressions.

*1096,A

Logical Error 1096:  Arithmetic error.

A "divide by zero" or similar situation was encountered when
evaluating an expression.

*1098,A

Syntax Error 1098:  Negative declaration not supported.

Negative (active-low) declarations are only supported in PIN and
NODE statements.

*1099,A

Syntax Error 1099:  Unsupported range.

A range (specified with the '..' operator) is bounded by
incompatible signals or numbers. Ranges must be specified that
results in 128 or fewer elements.

*1100,A

Syntax Error 1100:  Undeclared element 'xxxx' in range.

The expansion of a range expression resulted in the creation of a
previously undeclared element.

*1101,A

Syntax Error 1101:  Fuse number expected.

A number was expected that corresponds to a fuse location in the
previously declared device.

*1102,A

Syntax Error 1102:  Fuse value 1 or 0 expected.

A fuse value was expected. A value of 1 indicates an intact fuse,
and a value of 0 indicates a programmed ("blown") fuse.

*1103,A

Syntax Error 1103:  Unsupported nested set in state diagram header.

A non-symbolic state register must be specified as a set of signals,
and the set cannot be nested (contain other subsets).

*1104,A

Syntax Error 1104:  Dot extension 'xxxx' not supported in this
context.

The indicated dot extension is either unrecognized, or was used in
an unsupported manner. Dot extensions can only be applied to signals
or sets of signals.

*1105,A

Syntax Error 1105:  Signal label expected.

An identifier was used that is not a previously declared signal, and
a signal was expected.

*1109,A

Syntax Error 1109:  Register type of 'xxxx' does not match other set
elements.

State diagrams require matching register types. The state register
set specified contains signals of differing register types.

*1110,A

Syntax Error 1110:  Pin nn (VCC) cannot be used as input.

You have specified a device and pin number combination that cannot
be used as an input in your design.

*1111,A

Syntax Error 1111:  Pin nn (GND) cannot be used as input.

You have specified a device and pin number combination that cannot
be used as an input in your design.

*1112,A

Syntax Error 1112: Cannot use .FB or .Q as an output.

The .FB and .Q dot extensions are used for register feedback, and
are only supported on the right side of an equation.

*1113,A

Warning 1113:  ENABLE keyword obsolete - use .OE extension instead.

The ENABLE keyword is no longer supported in ABEL-HDL. Instead, you
should use the .OE dot extension to indicate a three-state output.

*1114,A

Syntax Error 1114:  'xxxx' attribute not supported for state
registers.

The indicated attribute is not supported for state registers.

*1116,A

Syntax Error 1116:  Multiple attribute list not supported in this
context.

You have used the '=' operator to specify signal attributes for
signals that have not been assigned pins. You should use the
'ISTYPE' attribute to assign attributes instead of the '=' operator.

*1118,A

Syntax Error 1118:  Module '%s' has already been declared.

The indicated submodule has already been declared in an INTERFACE
statement, or the identifier has already been defined as some other
type of declaration.

*1119,A

Syntax Error 1119:  Only one name is allowed in a group
declaration.

A GROUP declaration can only have a single group identifier.

*1120,A

Syntax Error 1120:  Only one device allowed.

Multiple device declarations are not supported in ABEL-HDL.

*1121,A

Syntax Error 1121:  Device declaration must be made before signal
declarations.

If a device declaration is made in the source file, it must be made
before any signal declarations.

*1122,A

Logical Error 1122:  Filename 'xxxx.xxx' too long.

The indicated filename is too long for the operating system.

*1123,A

Syntax Error 1123:  Partition name expected.

The PLACE IN statement requires that a partition name be specified.

*1124,A

Warning 1124: 'INVERT' or 'BUFFER' not specified for 'xxxx' -
assuming 'buffer'.

You have not specified whether the indicated output signal will have
an inversion between the state register and the associated output
pin.  No inversion is assumed, which may result in incorrect
operation if the design is implemented in a device with inverting
outputs.

*1125,A

Syntax Error:  'IN' expected.

The PLACE statement requires that a partition name be specified
using the PLACE IN syntax.

*1126,A

Warning 1126:  Cannot use ':=' operator with dot extensions.

The ':=' (clocked assignment) operator is used to describe the
operation of an registered output pin. If dot extensions are used,
you should use the '=' assignment operator, since dot extensions
(including register input ports) are inherently combinational.

*1128,A

Syntax Error 1128:  Cannot have operators in state register.

The state register set must consist of a set of signals, with no
complex operators.

*1129,A

Syntax Error 1129:  Cannot expand expression - possibly recursive
definition.

The ABEL compiler has detected a recursive constant declaration.
Check that you have not referenced the same identifier on both sides
of the '=' operator.

*1130,A

Syntax Error 1130:  Missing set element.

Set elements can consist of signals, numbers, special constants,
sets or expressions and are separated by commas. One of these items
was expected in the set.

*1131,A

Syntax Error 1131:  Missing set range element.

The '..' (set range) operator was used with no second boundary
element.

*1132,A

Syntax Error 1132:  Keyword IN not supported in this context.

Multiple device declarations and corresponding device-specific
sections are no longer supported in ABEL-HDL.  The IN keyword is
only supported in conjunction with the PLACE keyword.

*1133,A

Warning 1133:  Signal 'xxxx' is already type 'INVERT'.  Attribute
overridden.

The indicated signal has been previously declared as ISTYPE
'invert', or a device and pin number were specified that implied
'invert'.  The 'invert' attribute will be replaced by 'buffer'.

*1134,A

Warning 1134:  Signal 'xxxx' already defined as type 'BUFFER',

The indicated signal has been previously declared as ISTYPE
'buffer', or a device and pin number were specified that implied
'buffer'.  The 'buffer' attribute will be replaced by 'invert'.

*1135,A

Logical Error 1135:  Signal 'xxxx' is type 'input'.

The indicated signal was declared as an input, but was found on the
left side of an equation.  This error can occur if an output port of
a functional block is used on the left side of an equation.

*1136,A

Logical Error 1136:  Signal 'xxxx' is type 'output'.

The indicated signal was declared as an output, but was found on the
right side of an equation.  This error can occur if an input port of
a functional block is used on the right side of an equation.

*1139,A

Warning 1139:  Adding implied 'xxxx' equation for output 'xxxx'.

An equation is being generated for the indicated output due to
implied logic (clocks or output enables) in the target device.  The
use of implied clocks and enables is not recommended; you should add
the appropriate clock and enable equations to the design.

*1140,A

Syntax Error 1140:  State machine reset syntax not supported for
non-symbolic state diagram.

The SYNC_RESET and ASYNC_RESET statements are only supported in
symbolic state diagrams.

*1145,A

Syntax Error 1145:  Label 'xxxx' is already declared as a number.

An identifier that is declared as a number was used in a context in
which numbers were not supported.

*1148,A

Syntax Error 1148:  Only one name is supported in interface
declarations.

INTERFACE statements must have only one submodule name.

*1149,A

Syntax Error 1149:  Empty interface port list.

INTERFACE statements must include a module name and at least one
lower-level signal (port).

*1150,A

Syntax Error 1150:  Functional block 'xxxx' has already been
declared.

The indicated identifier has already been declared, and can't be
redefined as a functional block.

*1151,A

Warning 1151: Assuming 'buffer' for dot extension conversion.

A pin-to-pin dot extension is being converted to detailed syntax,
but there is no 'invert' or 'buffer' attribute specified.  The
conversion will be made with the assumption that the output will
not be inverted.  You should add a 'buffer' or 'invert' attribute
to ensure that the design works as expected.

*1152,A

Syntax Error 1152:  External module name expected.

The FUNCTIONAL_BLOCK statement requires a module name that has
previously been defined with an INTERFACE statement.

*1156,A

Syntax Error 1156: Functional block not supported without port
extension.

Functional block identifiers must always be combined with one or
more port names when used in logic descriptions.

*1157,A

Syntax Error 1157:  Specified port(s) not found for functional block
'xxxx'.

A port name has been specified with a functional block name, but the
port name was not found in the port list of the INTERFACE statement.

*1160,A

Syntax Error 1160:  Set index not supported here (must follow a set
or set name).

A set index was used in a place other than after a set or set
constant.  A set index must immediately follow the set or set
constant identifier.


*1161,A

Syntax Error 1161:  Set index not supported for set expression.

The set index contained index values that were not supported for the
set.

*1162,A

Syntax Error 1162:  '!' expected.

A set range was specified with a mismatch of active-level operators.

*1163,A

Syntax Error 1163:  '!' mismatch.

A set range was specified with a mismatch of active-level operators.

*1164,A

Syntax Error 1164:  ':' expected.

A colon was expected after a state diagram state value or symbolic
state identifier.

*1165,A

Fatal Error 1165:  Unable to merge truth table logic for one or more
outputs.

ABEL does not support the logic for an output to be defined using
multiple truth tables.  The truth tables for an output must be
combined into a single table.

*1166,A

Warning 1166:  Only one XOR factor equation is supported for each
output.

ABEL only supports one XOR factor equation for each output in
the design.  Additional XOR factor equations are ignored.

*1167,A

Logical Error 1167: Overlapping logic specified for output 'xxxx'.

The indicated output was used as a state diagram state register and
conflicting transition logic (non-exclusive IF-THEN logic, for
example) was specified.

*1168,A

Logical Error 1168:  Incomplete on, off and dc logic specified for
output 'xxxx'.

Design specifies specific on-set, off-set and don't care logic for
the indicated output, but the logic that you have specified is not
complete.  On-sets are entered using equations, truth tables and
state diagrams; off-sets are entered using state diagrams and truth
tables, and don't cares are entered using equations.

Remove either the on-set, off-set or don't care logic OR enter a
complete specification for all three types of logic.

*1169,A

Syntax Error 1169:  Set element type expected for @SETSIZE
directive.

Enter a set, or the name of a set, in the @SETSIZE directive.

*1170,A

Warning 1170:  No register type specified for 'xxxx' - setting to
'reg'.

Design does not specify a register type for the indicated output,
and the output was used in a way that implies a register.

Add a register type attribute such as 'reg_D', 'reg_T', to eliminate
the warning.

*1171,A

Syntax Error 1171:  No register type specified for state register.

A state diagram was written that requires a register type to be
specified.

Add a register type attribute such as 'reg', 'reg_D', 'reg_T', to 
eliminate the warning.

*1172,A

Syntax Error 1172:  No state register declared.

Design declares symbolic states using the STATE declaration keyword,
but does not declare a state register.

Declare a state register before declaring symbolic states.

*1173,A

Syntax Error 1173:  No states declared for 'xxxx'.

Design specifies a state diagram and state register, but does not 
declare any symbolic state identifiers.

Declare the symbolic states using the STATE declaration keyword.

*1174,A

Syntax Error 1174:  Assignment to state register not supported. 

State registers may only be used with dot extensions such as .CLK
(to specify the logic for a state machine clock). Design cannot 
specify an equation using the symbolic state name as an output.

Use a state diagram to define the logic for the state register.

*1178,A

Warning 1178:  Signal 'xxxx' is already 'pos'. Attribute will be
overridden.

The indicated output has already been assigned an attribute that
conflicts with the attribute entered, or design specifies a device
and pin number that implies a conflicting attribute. The attribute
specified in the design will take precedence.

*1179,A

Warning 1179:  Signal 'xxxx' is already 'neg'. Attribute will be
overridden.

The indicated output has already been assigned an attribute that
conflicts with the attribute entered, or design specifies a device
and pin number that implies a conflicting attribute. The attribute
specified in the design will take precedence.

*1180,A

Warning 1180:  Signal 'xxxx' is already 'dc'. Attribute will be
overridden.

The indicated output has already been assigned an attribute that
conflicts with the attribute entered, or design specifies a device
and pin number that implies a conflicting attribute. The attribute
specified in the design will take precedence.
*1181,A

Warning 1181:  Signal 'xxxx' is already 'reg'. Attribute will be
overridden.

The indicated output has already been assigned an attribute that
conflicts with the attribute entered, or design specifies a device
and pin number that implies a conflicting attribute. The attribute
specified in the design will take precedence.

*1182,A

Warning 1182:  Signal 'xxxx' is already 'com'. Attribute will be
overridden.

The indicated output has already been assigned an attribute that
conflicts with the attribute entered, or design specifies a device
and pin number that implies a conflicting attribute. The attribute
specified in the design will take precedence.

